    'chest-drain': { zh: '胸管引流', en: 'Intercostal chest drain', text: '在安全三角（腋中線第 4–5 肋間）置入胸管接水封瓶：氣胸時肺重新貼合、M 型恢復海岸徵；血胸用大口徑管，初次引流 >1500 mL 或每小時 >200 mL 持續數小時需開胸。', textEn: 'A drain in the safe triangle (4th–5th space, mid-axillary line) connected to an underwater seal: in pneumothorax the lung re-apposes and M-mode returns to the seashore sign; for haemothorax a large-bore tube is used, and more than 1500 mL at once or over 200 mL an hour for several hours calls for thoracotomy.' },
    pci: { zh: '直接 PCI 流程', en: 'Primary PCI pathway', text: '確認 STEMI 後啟動導管室，到院至打通血管目標 ≤90 分鐘（轉院者首次醫療接觸 ≤120 分鐘，否則先溶栓）；以支架打通梗塞相關血管後 ST 段明顯回落，延遲到院者 Q 波可能保留。', textEn: 'Once STEMI is confirmed the catheter laboratory is activated, aiming for door-to-balloon within 90 minutes (first medical contact within 120 minutes for transfers, otherwise thrombolysis first); stenting the culprit artery makes the ST segments resolve, although Q waves may remain if presentation was late.' },
    defib: { zh: '電擊去顫', en: 'Defibrillation', text: '可電擊節律（VF／無脈性 VT）立即電擊，之後馬上繼續 CPR 兩分鐘再評估；電擊讓所有心肌同時去極化，竇房結得以重新主導，恢復自發循環時可見有組織的節律、脈波與 EtCO₂ 上升。', textEn: 'A shockable rhythm (VF or pulseless VT) is shocked at once, followed immediately by two minutes of CPR before the next rhythm check; the shock depolarises the whole myocardium so the sinus node can take over, and ROSC appears as an organised rhythm with a pulse wave and rising EtCO₂.' },
    cpr: { zh: '高品質 CPR', en: 'High-quality CPR', text: '每分鐘 100–120 次、深度 5–6 cm、完全回彈並減少中斷；按壓維持冠狀動脈與腦部灌流，EtCO₂ ≥10–20 mmHg 代表有效，但 CPR 本身不會把 VF 轉回竇性心律。', textEn: 'Compressions at 100–120 a minute, 5–6 cm deep, with full recoil and minimal interruption keep the coronary and cerebral circulation going; an EtCO₂ of 10–20 mmHg or more indicates effective CPR, but CPR alone does not convert VF to sinus rhythm.' },
    tevar: { zh: '主動脈內支架（TEVAR）', en: 'Thoracic endovascular repair (TEVAR)', text: '經股動脈置入覆膜支架覆蓋峽部撕裂，已取代多數開胸修補；術後胸片見沿降主動脈的支架網格，縱膈血腫需數週吸收。', textEn: 'A covered stent graft delivered through the femoral artery seals the isthmus tear and has replaced most open repairs; the post-operative film shows the stent mesh along the descending aorta, and the mediastinal haematoma takes weeks to resorb.' },
    'anti-impulse': { zh: '控制心跳與血壓', en: 'Anti-impulse therapy', text: '以短效 β 阻斷劑等降低心跳與收縮壓，減少對撕裂主動脈壁的剪力，爭取做 CT 與修補的時間；這不會改變胸片。', textEn: 'A short-acting beta-blocker and similar agents lower heart rate and systolic pressure, reducing shear on the torn aortic wall and buying time for CT and repair; it does not change the chest film.' }
